- op: discuss  # 7e5a
  at: '2026-10-22T03:21:16Z'  # 7e5a
  by: agent  # 7e5a
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 7e5a
  clock: 5  # 7e5a
  nonce: 7e5a  # 7e5a
  message: "Fixed in PR #1797 (dev e9215548f6). DefUseResult/CfgStatement gain targets (LHS by position, blank kept as '_'); Go short-var and assignment handlers report it when a blank is present and every other target names exactly one variable; stmt_defuse uses it, so _received_seeds maps the received position exactly. Repro through the production CLI (fresh cache), claim host_secret -> subprocess, fixture get() returns os.Getenv at position 0; wrap() does '_, err := get(); return \"ls\", err'; main() does 'name, err := wrap(); exec.Command(name, err.Error()).Run()': BEFORE (dev e3ea9db6c9) exit 1, violated, 2 evidence rows with source_returned_by [wrap, get] -- the error-chain climb; AFTER (merged dev) exit 3, confirmed_with_caveats, 0 evidence. Control (value, _ := get(); return value, nil) stays violated with returned_by {get, wrap} (test_go_a_blank_elsewhere_keeps_the_value_s_position). Corpus: 0 verdicts moved on runc/gin/coredns/buildah; buildah walks 2874 -> 2749, host-secret-no-network evidence 91 -> 79. NOT COVERED: 'var _, err = f()' spec declarations; a target naming no variable (*p) keeps the seed-everything fallback."  # 7e5a
